Uuls has another small problem.  The readdir() routine defines needbytes
as a long, but  &needbytes is passed to fread(),  which  expects an int.
This might cause  trouble on machines  where int == short.  The solution
is to make  needbytes an int.  (I'll fix the master  source for the next
time I release it to the Net, if ever.)

